;
; virtio_wddm_rs.inf - 983 = 982 KMD + Turnip WSI present thread / linear swapchain.
; KMD = 976 accounting (3 nodes, BlobHost3D, no Graphics GpuMmu).
; Turnip ARM64/ARM64EC = 983: GDI present on its own thread + linear swapchain image (no per-frame buffer blit). KMD 982 unchanged.
;
; 984: UMD file logging default off, opt-in via VIRTIO_WDDM_LOG_FILE; per-present logs demoted to VERBOSE
; 985: WSI present: tiled+blit default, present thread, no same-queue CPU wait before submit, single SetDIBitsToDevice, fault->DEVICE_LOST (TU_WSI_LINEAR/TU_WIN_SUBMIT_CPU_WAIT/TU_WSI_GDI_DIB for A/B)
; 986: WSI present: DIB section back to default (SetDIBitsToDevice direct path measured no gain, TU_WSI_GDI_DIRECT=1 for A/B); present thread + no same-queue CPU wait before submit + fault->DEVICE_LOST kept from 985
; 987: P0 diagnostics build (KMD_DIAGNOSTICS=1): count blt present local-copy eligibility and last-seen blob formats/strides in Bringup registry; no behavior change (kmd-blt-present-plan.md P0)
; 988: P0 diagnostics round 2: eligibility classifier accepts MAP_COHERENT 3D dst (standard allocation), records dst kind/flags/layout stride; counts standard allocation types. No behavior change.
; 989: P1 blt present local copy (diagnostics build): src linear guest blob + dst STAGINGSURFACE 3D -> KMD memcpy with R/B swizzle on the handler thread, no virtio traffic; PresentLocalCopy=0 registry kill switch
; 990: P1 local copy + fence-level diagnostics (submit/run/done fence slots, periodic publish from the handler thread); investigating present hang on 989
; 991: P1 diag: record which side/status fails kernel mapping (990 showed MapFail on every eligible present, virgl fallback works)
; 992: P1: dst kernel mapping via IoAllocateMdl+PFN fill (MmAllocateMdlForIoSpace rejects RAM ranges -> every eligible present hit MapFail on 990/991)
; 993: P1: Cached CPU mapping for CpuVisible 3D standard allocations (DXGI Lock readback of the staging surface was 4.2 ms/frame uncached); copy/wait time sums in diagnostics
; 994: P1 release build (no bringup diagnostics): blt present local copy + Cached staging surfaces; 1164x681 blt 92 -> 334-381 fps (flip 432), window readback 0 errors
; 995: D3D12 UMD dx12um_virtio (P1 skeleton), slot 3; D3D12Enable default 1
; 996: D3D12 UMD P1: CreateDevice passes runtime validation (depth format bits, MSAA levels, row-major alignment)
; 997: D3D12 P2: heaps/resources, descriptors, root signatures, DXIL-container PSOs, command lists, queue fence bridge (scheme C)
; 998: D3D12 P2: IAT tracer for the runtime's D3DKMT sync calls (VIRTIO_WDDM_LOG_KMT=1)
; 999: D3D12 P2 fix: single runtime queue context (broadcast signal completes on the first context; probe bcast/gatesignal evidence)
; 1000: D3D12 P2: KMT tracer now hooks d3dkmt delay imports by ordinal
; 1001: D3D12 P2: KMT tracer hooks d3dkmt delay imports by ordinal (1000 was stale)
; 1002: D3D12 P2 diag: per-ECL log + timestamped KMT trace
; 1003: D3D12 P2 diag: log 3D RTV args
; 1004: D3D12 P2 diag: log rtv/clear handle addresses
; 1005: D3D12 P2 diag: dump rtv desc slot before/after vkd3d write
; 1006: D3D12 P2 diag: detect unwritten rtv desc
; 1007: D3D12: resolve committed buffer heap size sentinel before allocation
; 1008: DXIL: handle switches without a common post-dominator
; 1009: D3D12: accept stream output declarations without GS bytecode
; 1010: D3D12: match DXIL stream outputs using DDI register coordinates
; 1011: fix resolveIsNanCheck unary operand bounds
; 1012: guard unary FIsNan in resolveIdentityCompareOp
; 1013: guard unary identity compare operands
; 1014: diagnose NIR source insertion validation
; 1015: identify ir3 NIR pass corrupting cs_uav_store
; 1016: diagnose null NIR SSA source
; 1017: handle missing SPIR-V function call scalar SSA with undef
; 1018: diagnose direct UDiv call null parameter
; 1019: diagnose NIR null source object layout
; 1020: fill missing SPIR-V call parameters with typed undef
; 1021: return invalid shader when SPIR-V to NIR conversion fails
; 1022: inline SPIR-V helper functions before Turnip lowering
; 1023: fix typed undefined SPIR-V call arguments without function inlining
; 1024: fix missing scalar SPIR-V call arguments with typed undef
; 1025: diagnose remaining NIR NULL source
; 1026: diagnose NIR NULL source in add_defs_uses
; 1027: fix missing composite SPIR-V call argument leaves
; 1028: diagnose missing SPIR-V call parameter type
; 1029: inline repaired typed SPIR-V helper call arguments
; 1030: inline helper calls after lowering returns and initializers
; 1031: lower typed helper undef arguments to zero before IR3
; 1032: lower compute helper undef arguments before IR3
; 1033: use typed zero for missing SPIR-V helper arguments
; 1034: Log SPIR-V conversion errors for compute pipeline failures
; 1035: Fix malformed SPIR-V UDiv helper types
; 1036: Fix stale ARM64EC entrypoint object rebuild and restore Turnip ICD
; 1037: MapHeap: keep committed UNKNOWN-layout textures undisclosed without reporting a DDI failure
; 1038: 3D image copy, blit, and clear use the r3d path
; 1039: Turnip: keep 3D clear layer at zero when each slice is selected by the MRT base
; 1040: Turnip: route unaligned 3D texture uploads through 3D blit ops
; 1041: A8XX TEX_LINE_OFFSET is expressed in bits; fix 3D buffer upload pitch
; 1042: D24 copy diagnostics: log copy locations, barriers, and command-list HRESULT
; 1043: D24 trace: log DSV creation, depth clear, and dispatch entry points
; 1044: D3D12 allocation info: map tight alignment and preserve invalid allocation sentinel
; 1045: Record EXT_dgc stage mask for ExecuteIndirect diagnostics
; 1046: DX12 default enabled; restore compute ExecuteIndirect fallback when EXT_dgc is unavailable
; 1047: ExecuteIndirect compute fallback: lower compute root state through per-dispatch UBO when DGC is unavailable
; 1048: ExecuteIndirect compute fallback: honor predication in state-template dispatches
; 1049: ExecuteIndirect compute fallback: preserve command ordering and root state rebinding
; 1050: ExecuteIndirect compute template cleanup: release DGC buffers only when created
; 1052: Restore buffer DDI data size after allocation info experiment
; 1053: P3 D3D12 primary allocation and flip present
; 1054: P3 use D3D12 allocation callbacks for primary
; 1055: P3 single-context D3D12 flip present
; 1056: P3 primary lifetime and current refresh rate
; 1057: D3D12 P3 primary resource retirement and present logging cleanup
; 1058: P4 queue shutdown and VirtIO reset ordering
; 1059: P4 reset epoch: gate stale channels and rebuild VirtIO queues after TDR
; 1061: P4 TDR reset breadcrumb stages for callback, worker join, VirtIO reset, and restart
; 1062: D3D12: implement calibrated GPU clock from QPC
; 1063: D3D12 resource allocation span sizing trial
; 1064: D3D12 allocation layout diagnostic
; 1065: D3D12 allocation alignment diagnostic
; 1066: D3D12 resource allocation alignment fixes
; 1067: D3D12 resource allocation: clamp buffer resource alignment to 64 KiB
; 1068: translate DDI heap properties and normalize buffer allocation queries
; 1069: Report unsupported CPU-visible depth texture as invalid request
; 1070: Restore validated 1068 resource behavior
; 1071: Remove allocation query debug logging
; 1072: Map committed texture from vkd3d CPU staging memory
; 1073: Expose CPU staging layout for committed textures
; 1074: Restore validated D3D12 resource path; keep DX12 enabled
; 1075: D3D12 recover small placed texture alignment from validated allocation info
; 1077: Retain validated small texture alignment; withdraw ineffective MSAA caps experiment
; 1078: D3D12 implement pipeline library storage serialization and reload
; 1079: D3D12 translate tessellation factor semantic indices
; 1080: Allow unnamed passthrough hull shader entry during quirk lookup
; 1086: restore verified UMD after failed alignment experiment
; 1087: Report 16-bit minimum shader precision for non-native min16float pipelines.
; 1088: Advertise gapless SM 6.2 for non-native FP16 DXIL pipelines and 16-bit minimum precision.
; 1089: Allow GPU_UPLOAD depth textures through the staging-copy path.
; 1090: Preserve GPU_UPLOAD heap type for depth texture staging copies
; 1097: Restore validated 1090 UMD after unsuccessful Map experiments
; 1098: D3D12 DDI 0041: report 64 KiB MSAA placement support
; 1099: MapHeap: expose vkd3d CPU staging address for custom textures
; 1100: MapHeap: use vkd3d CPU staging address for custom textures; restore ARM64X entry point
; 1101: Map custom CPU textures through a vkd3d placed heap span
; 1102: Reject unsupported CPU-visible committed textures without a runtime KMT mapping
; 1103: Reject CPU-visible committed COMMON textures without a runtime KMT mapping
; 1104: Reject CPU-visible committed COMMON textures with E_INVALIDARG when runtime KMT mapping is unavailable
; 1105: Report programmable sample positions tier 1 to unlock MSAA resources born in RESOLVE_DEST
; 1106: Forward ClearState to the inner command list so root constants stop leaking across ClearState
; 1107: Give the runtime the real host pointer and inner subresource layout for CPU-visible heap textures
; 1108: Report row-major texture support: CPU-visible heap textures are linear host memory, unlocking runtime Map(NULL)
; 1109: Also report 64K standard swizzle to open the runtime Map(NULL) gate
; 1110: Revert the texture layout caps experiment: keep the host pointer and layout plumbing, gates stay off
; 1111: EXPERIMENT: MapHeap fails for CPU-visible committed textures
; 1112: KMT trace: enumerate the runtime's D3DKMT delay imports
; 1113: KMT trace: wrap CreateAllocation and Lock
; 1114: KMT trace: wrap CreateAllocation and Lock
; 1115: Route CPU-visible committed textures through the runtime allocator to mint a KMT allocation
; 1116: Reuse the ICD's blob in the committed-texture allocation
; 1117: Wrap CPU-visible committed textures in pSystemMem KMT allocations
; 1118: Wrap CPU-visible committed textures in pSystemMem KMT allocations
; 1119: Wrap CPU-visible committed textures in pSystemMem KMT allocations
; 1120: Call the D3D12 AllocateCb variant for the sysmem wrap
; 1121: Gate the sysmem wrap behind VIRTIO_WDDM_SYSMEM_WRAP=1
; 1122: Log the sysmem wrap gate decision
; 1123: Give the sysmem wrap an aperture residency segment
; 1124: Wrap lazily from MapHeap where the runtime resource handle is live
; 1125: Wrap lazily from MapHeap where the runtime resource handle is live
; 1127: Restore clean D3D12 UMD after resolve diagnostics
; 1129: Restore clean resolve path; WARP reproduces renderpass array layer 1 failure
; 1130: Preserve explicit byte address wrapping on Turnip
; 1131: Honor literal drirc engine alternatives without a regex library
; 1132: Use EXT primitive restart index for D3D12 strip cut values
; 1133: Honor strip cut values independently of index format
; 1134: Support sliced 3D storage image views in Turnip
; 1135: Use explicit attachment clears under native conditional rendering
; 1136: Predicate single-sample color texture CopyResource through GPU scratch buffers
; 1137: Preserve destination bytes for predicated direct color resolves
; 1138: Expand custom border color storage and advertised limit to 8192 entries
; 1139: Pad experimental sysmem allocation request to common KMD envelope
; 1140: Keep sysmem wrappers local and retire runtime allocation before backing
; 1141: Return existing resource kernel allocation handles
; 1142: Associate experimental sysmem backing during resource creation
; 1143: Report linear CPU texture staging layout to runtime
; 1144: Select CPU linear layout before native resource creation
; 1145: Upload native runtime CPU texture writes when unmapping
; 1146: Flush CPU staging writes and upload textures at native heap unmap
; 1147: Submit native CPU texture uploads before releasing resource ownership
; 1148: Publish persistently mapped texture writes before command execution
; 1149: Wrap scalar raw-buffer component addresses before descriptor robustness
; 1150: Align Windows GPU virtual address reservations to 64 KiB
; 1151: Use 64 KiB chunked backing directly for BOs of 2 MiB or larger
; 1152: Implement DDI 0098 argument and function table bridge for independent devices
; 1154: Rollback unverified 1153 runtime buffer and global allocation bridge experiment; restore exact 1152 binaries for AIO hang investigation
; 1155: Prevent flip DPC preemption deadlock by raising IRQL around async queue producer lock
; 1156: Clear root arguments without discarding the initial graphics pipeline
; 1163: Recovery package restoring user-confirmed AIO baseline 1156 after ExecuteIndirect diagnostic timeout; not deployed
; 1164: ExecuteIndirect graphics fallback candidate without temporary diagnostics, ARM64 only
; 1165: Block render-pass resume across ExecuteIndirect GPU parameter patch dispatch
; 1166: ExecuteIndirect graphics root-state fallback on both architectures; vbo_offsets ARM64 28/0; vkd3d 7dda3395
; 1167: Use raw root CBV addresses for GPU ExecuteIndirect state fallback without DGC
; 1168: Expose RGBA8 alongside BGRA8 VidPN source modes for DXGI mode enumeration
; 1170: Restore 1168 RGBA8 candidate for continued 3DMark diagnosis per user request
; 1171: D3D9On12: stage ordinary present surfaces in runtime allocations
; 1172: D3D9On12: retire blt present copy before entering kernel present
; 1173: D3D9On12: runtime-backed shareable render targets for FLIPEX
; 1174: Add x86 D3D12 UMD, Vulkan loader and Turnip for system D3D9On12
; 1175: Declare no native D3D9 UMD so Windows selects system D3D9On12 without application proxies
; 1180: Copy WDDM commands into queue-owned DMA buffers before publication
; 1181: Diagnostic: audit WDDM physical DMA addresses and submission ranges
; 1182: Diagnostic: compare original WDDM DMA bytes on host and guest before completion
; 1183: Diagnostic: correlate DMA completion addresses, hashes and ARM translation attributes
; 1184: Stage WDDM DMA commands in a reusable cached arena until virtqueue completion
; 1185: Add x86 D3D10/11 UMD and system Vulkan/OpenGL ICD registration
; 1186: Complete WoW OpenGL ICD version and flags
; 1190: Restore 1186 baseline after inconclusive residency experiments
; 1192: Restore production baseline after passive fence diagnostics
; 1193: Diagnostic: bound UMA UMD memory pool chunks to 32 MiB
; 1194: Apply verified UMA UMD 32 MiB chunk policy to ARM64EC and x86
; 1195: Diagnostic: release empty UMA UMD pool chunks without retention
; 1196: UMA UMD residency fixes: bounded chunks and prompt empty-chunk reclamation on all architectures
; 1198: Diagnostic KMD BlobHost3D local budget accounting; revert native 8MiB experiment
; 1199: Diagnostic guest aperture non-local budget group; host blobs remain local
; 1211: UMD: submit deferred private-image clears before command-list completion
; 1212: UMD: flush RTV clear immediately to release destroyed WebGL images
; 1213: UMD: retain imported Vulkan image ownership until DXVK releases queued references
; 1214: UMD: flush private-image clears at command-list completion; no imported handle ownership change
; 1215: diagnostic image create/destroy logging only
; 1216: vdrm diagnostics: trace BO creation and close via DebugView
; 1217: Rebuild current rolled-back sources for Aquarium fullscreen baseline; not a leak fix
; 1219: Drain D3D11 runtime deferred destruction at Present and Flush
; 1220: Submit pending offscreen clears at UMD command boundaries

[Version]
Signature="$Windows NT$"
Class=Display
ClassGUID={4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}
Provider=%ManufacturerName%
DriverVer=10/03/2026,20.15.1.1220
CatalogFile=virtio_wddm_rs.cat
PnpLockdown=1

[DestinationDirs]
VirtioGpu_Files.Driver = 13
VirtioGpu_Files.Usermode = 13

[SourceDisksNames]
1 = %DiskId1%,,,""

[SourceDisksFiles]
freedreno_icd.x86.json = 1,,
droidvm_opengl_x86.dll = 1,,
dx11um_virtio_x86.dll = 1,,
vulkan_freedreno_x86.dll = 1,,
droidvm_vulkan_x86.dll = 1,,
dx12um_virtio_x86.dll = 1,,
virtio_wddm_rs.sys = 1,,
dx11um_virtio.dll = 1,,
dx11um_virtio_arm64.dll = 1,,
dx11um_virtio_arm64ec.dll = 1,,
